{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"Committed 4755c79bd9bd0b159c1397e547d01e5f43f91093; 17/17 passing (was 16/17). Root cause for subtest 11 'git rebase with failed pick': the internal pick path cherry_pick_for_rebase (grit/src/commands/rebase.rs) ran only preflight_cherry_pick_cwd_obstruction (cwd-removal + submodule cases), missing the general 'newly-added entry would overwrite an untracked working-tree file' guard that the standalone cherry-pick command already has. So 'exec >G' then 'pick G' silently overwrote the untracked file instead of aborting. Fix: added super::reset::check_untracked_cherry_pick_obstruction(wt, &old_index, &merged_index) before the index/worktree write in the full-merge pick path. It inspects only stage-0 new paths present untracked on disk, conflict-safe, and bails before any mutation so --continue retries cleanly (test relies on 4 retries). Regression checks all green: t3403 20/20, t3407 17/17, t3417 4/4, t3418 30/30, t3429 7/7, t3510 55/55; t3404 unchanged-to-improved."}